  "identifier": "nsclc-brainmet-time",
  "name": "Compartment-Resolved Spatial Transcriptomics of the NSCLC Tumour Immune Microenvironment",
  "description": "A reproducible Snakemake workflow reanalysing NanoString GeoMx DSP WTA profiles (GEO GSE200563; 120 AOIs, 35 NSCLC patients plus 7 non-tumour brain controls) to compare the tumour immune microenvironment of primary NSCLC lung tumours with matched brain metastases, resolved by tissue compartment. The brain immune compartment is n = 8 AOIs, which detects roughly 1.1-1.3 SD at 80% power, so a null result is uninformative rather than negative. The assay carries no coordinates, so cross-compartment findings are inferred crosstalk between adjacent compartments, never colocalisation. A learning and methods project, not intended for peer-reviewed publication.",
